1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,850
We all know the importance of education.
我们都知道教育的重要性。

2
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:15,760
Everyone aspires to have a good one, but its quality and availability is not the same for all.
每个人都渴望接受良好的教育，但教育的质量与是否可以接受教育却因人而异。

3
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:26,630
This situation changes as social, economic and political conditions change and technological development provides new benefits and threats.
随着社会、经济、政治环境的变化，再加上技术发展带来的新益处与新挑战，这种情况也在不断改变。

4
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:42,890
The Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), which promotes policies that will improve the economic and social well-being of people around the world, has been looking at the future of global education.
经济合作与发展组织（经合组织）一直致力于推动各类政策，以提升全球人民的经济与社会福祉，该组织目前正在研究全球教育的未来发展趋势。

5
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:54,290
Its head of education, Andreas Schleicher, has been talking to the BBC about some major international trends affecting education systems around the world.
其教育部门负责人安德烈亚斯·施莱歇尔在接受英国广播公司采访时，谈到了影响全球教育体系的几大国际趋势。

6
00:00:54,290 --> 00:01:03,730
One threat is the widening gap between rich and poor, with more intense pockets of extreme privilege and deprivation.
其中一个挑战是贫富差距的不断扩大，极端特权与极端贫困的群体分化愈发明显。

7
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:12,520
In OECD countries, the richest 10% have incomes 10 times greater than the poorest 10%.
在经合组织成员国中，最富有的10%人群的收入是最贫穷的10%人群的十倍。

8
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:21,380
This inequality is a challenge for schools who want to offer equal and fair access to education for everyone.
这种不平等现象，对致力于为所有人提供平等、公平教育机会的学校而言，是一项巨大挑战。

9
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:25,200
Another trend is the rising affluence in Asia.
另一个趋势是亚洲地区富裕程度的不断提升。

10
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:33,750
It's suggested that a large rise in the middle-classes in China and India will increase demand for university places.
有观点认为，中国和印度的中产阶级规模大幅扩大，将会增加对大学入学名额的需求。

11
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:41,260
Andreas Schleicher asks the question "What values will these newly wealthy consumers want from their schools?"
安德烈亚斯·施莱歇尔提出了这样一个问题：“这些新晋富裕群体希望从学校中获得怎样的价值观？”

12
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:46,140
Increasing migration will also have an impact on education systems.
移民人数的不断增加也会对教育体系产生影响。

13
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:52,980
Mobility results in more culturally diverse students eager to learn and develop a good life for themselves.
人口流动带来了更多文化背景多元的学生，这些学生渴望通过学习为自己创造美好的生活。

14
00:01:52,980 --> 00:02:01,280
But that can be a challenge, too, as Andreas Schleicher asks: "How should schools support pupils arriving from around the world?
但这同时也是一项挑战，正如安德烈亚斯·施莱歇尔所提出的：“学校应如何为来自世界各地的学生提供支持？

15
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:05,360
What questions does it raise about identity and integration?
这会引发哪些关于身份认同与社会融入的问题？

16
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:09,550
Will schools have a bigger role in teaching about shared values?"
学校在传授共同价值观方面是否应该承担更重要的角色？”

17
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:20,340
Funding pressure is another issue: as our demand and expectation for education rises and more people go to university, who's going to pay for it all?
资金压力是另一个亟待解决的问题：随着人们对教育的需求与期望不断提升，越来越多的人进入大学深造，那么谁来为这一切买单？

18
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,360
The rise in dependency on technology is another concern.
对技术的依赖程度日益加深也是另一个令人担忧的问题。

19
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:29,710
What should students learn when many of their talents can be replicated by machines?
当人类的诸多才能都能被机器复刻时，学生们应该学习些什么？

20
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:33,310
And how reliant should we be on learning from the internet?
我们又该在多大程度上依赖网络学习？

21
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:37,870
These are just some of the issues the OECD is highlighting.
以上只是经合组织着重强调的部分问题。

22
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:51,780
But they remain irrelevant for hundreds of millions of the world's poorest children who don't even have access to school places or receive such low-quality education that they leave without the most basic literacy or numeracy.
但对于全球数亿最贫困的儿童来说，这些问题却毫无意义——他们甚至没有入学机会，或是接受的教育质量极低，毕业时连最基础的读写和计算能力都不具备。
